# Agent-in-Box Guest Worker service overrides.
#
# systemd reads this file as root before starting the unprivileged aib-worker
# service. Keep it root-owned and not group/other writable.
#
# NEVER place Provider API keys, Model Broker tokens, RPC bearer tokens, or
# other long-lived secrets in this file. The worker RPC bearer token lives in
# the separate file named by AGENT_IN_BOX_WORKER_TOKEN_FILE and is injected by
# controlled provisioning.

# Optional: Pi extension that implements the Computer Use tools. The installer
# also supports --cua-extension, which installs the file and a systemd drop-in.
# AGENT_IN_BOX_CUA_EXTENSION=/opt/agent-in-box/extensions/cua-extension.js

# Optional: Guest Agent endpoint used by that extension. A Guest Agent token is
# distinct from the worker RPC token and from the Model Broker token. The
# extension and its provisioning mechanism decide how to read that token from a
# protected file; never place the token value itself in this file.
# AGENT_IN_BOX_GUEST_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7611
# AGENT_IN_BOX_GUEST_TOKEN_FILE=/etc/agent-in-box/worker/guest-agent.token
